---
/**
 * Contribute — /contribute/  (IA v3 §11)
 *
 * The honest ask: free, open source, forever; all work happens GitHub-flow.
 * Issue numbers in the wireframe were placeholders — we link to the live
 * good-first-issue filter rather than fabricate specific issues.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getAllPlatforms } from '../../lib/platforms';

// Count of machines in the manifest — keep this honest-ask figure in step with the
// home page, which derives the same number rather than hard-coding it.
const machineCount = (await getAllPlatforms()).length;

const ORG = 'https://github.com/code198x';
const GOOD_FIRST = 'https://github.com/search?q=org%3Acode198x+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22+state%3Aopen&type=issues';
const OPEN_PRS = 'https://github.com/search?q=org%3Acode198x+is%3Apr+is%3Aopen&type=pullrequests';
// The low-friction route in. A PR is a high bar for a first contact, and the
// people who can test on real hardware or spot a wrong fact are not always the
// people who want to open one.
const DISCORD = 'https://discord.gg/AdmEYQKWZb';

const steps = [
  ['1', 'File an issue', 'Describe the work, attach references.'],
  ['2', 'Discuss', 'Scope, methodology fit, who owns it.'],
  ['3', 'Open a PR', 'Code, prose and assets in one branch.'],
  ['4', 'Merge → ship', 'Live on the site within days.'],
];
const deal = [
  'Every page free to read — no ads, no paywalls',
  'Every code sample MIT-licensed',
  'Every lesson binary is built and run before it is treated as true',
  'Every repo public · CC-BY for the prose',
  'If the project dies, the content survives',
];
const ways = [
  ['Port the methodology', "to a machine I don't own"],
  ['Author a game', 'on a machine you love'],
  ['Fill a vault entry', 'for a person, game, or chip'],
  ['Submit a pattern', 'with working code + screenshots'],
  ['Test on real iron', 'and attach photos to a PR'],
  ['Illustrate', 'make this look like a 1985 magazine'],
  ['Edit', 'catch the typos, tighten the prose'],
];
---

<Layout title="Contribute" description="Code Like It's 198x is community-built — free, open source, forever. Help port a machine, author a game, fill the Vault, or submit a pattern.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="ghost">HELP</div>
    <span class="wanted">WANTED</span>

    <div class="vhead">
      <p class="eyebrow">An honest ask</p>
      <h1>I can't build all<br />of this alone.</h1>
      <div class="herorule"></div>
      <p class="lede">The ambition is <span class="mk">≈ {machineCount} machines · dozens of games each · four decades</span>{' '}
        of context. One person could deliver one machine's worth in a decade. The work happens on
        <span class="mono">github.com/code198x</span> — issues for ideas, discussions for design, pull
        requests for the work — but you do not have to start there. If you would rather ask a question
        than open a pull request, <a href={DISCORD} rel="noopener">the Discord</a> is where to do it.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="how">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <div class="steps">
        {steps.map(([n, t, blurb], i) => (
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-h"><span class="num">{n}</span><span class="t">{t}</span>{i < 3 && <span class="arrow">→</span>}</div>
            <p>{blurb}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="two">
      <div class="card deal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The deal</p>
        <h2>Free. Open source.<br />Forever.</h2>
        <ul class="ticks">{deal.map(d => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="fine mono">github.com/code198x · archive available</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card ways">
        <p class="eyebrow">Ways to help</p>
        <h2>Pick an issue.<br />Open a PR.</h2>
        <ul class="waylist">{ways.map(([t, rest]) => <li><strong>{t}</strong> {rest}</li>)}</ul>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={GOOD_FIRST} rel="noopener">Open a good-first-issue →</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={DISCORD} rel="noopener">Ask in Discord</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={OPEN_PRS} rel="noopener">Browse open PRs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="issues">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open issues right now</p>
      <div class="issues-cta">
        <p>Every machine's port, every empty Vault entry, every wanted pattern is a real, open GitHub issue.
          Watch one, weigh in on the approach, or claim it. If none of them is the thing you know about,
          say what is — a machine you owned, a magazine you kept, a game you can still finish from memory
          is worth more here than an afternoon of someone else guessing.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={GOOD_FIRST} rel="noopener">See what's open ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="three">
      <div class="mini"><p class="eyebrow">What you get</p><p>Your name in <a href="/colophon">the colophon</a>, credit on what you wrote, and a say in how your machine is taught.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><p class="eyebrow">What you won't get</p><p>Money. Equity. A vesting schedule. This is a craft project, not a startup.</p></div>
      <div class="mini"><p class="eyebrow">The bar</p><p>Working code, clear sources, honest screenshots, and prose that says what was actually checked. <a href="/standards">Read the standards.</a></p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap { position: relative; max-width: var(--container-max-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-6) var(--space-16); overflow: hidden; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-family-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .mono { font-family: var(--font-family-mono); }

  .ghost { position: absolute; top: 40px; right: -20px; font-family: var(--font-family-read); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(180px, 30vw, 360px); line-height: 0.7; color: var(--color-house); opacity: 0.05; pointer-events: none; z-index: 0; transform: rotate(-4deg); }
  .wanted { position: absolute; top: 28px; right: 40px; z-index: 2; font-family: var(--font-family-mono); font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; border: 3px solid var(--color-house-2); color: var(--color-house-2); padding: 4px 14px; transform: rotate(-8deg); background: var(--color-surface); }

  .vhead { position: relative; z-index: 1; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
  .vhead h1 { font-family: var(--font-family-read); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 8vw, 5rem); line-height: 0.9;
      /* Reserve the descender the tight line-height does not: Literata's ink
         drops ~0.33em past the box, which collided with the strapline. */
      padding-bottom: 0.25em; margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; color: var(--color-text); }
  .herorule { height: 9px; width: 200px; max-width: 70%; background: var(--color-house); position: relative; margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; }
  .herorule::after { content: ""; position: absolute; right: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 24%; background: var(--color-house-2); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 72ch; margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; color: var(--color-text); }
  .lede a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.15em; }
  .mk { background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 58%, var(--color-house-tint) 58%); padding: 0 2px; }

  section { position: relative; z-index: 1; margin-top: var(--space-8); }

  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .step { position: relative; border: 3px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); padding: var(--space-4); }
  .step-h { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 6px; }
  .step .num { font-family: var(--font-family-read); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.8rem; color: var(--color-house-2); }
  .step .t { font-weight: 800; font-size: 1rem; }
  .step .arrow { position: absolute; right: -12px; top: 12px; font-family: var(--font-family-mono); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .step p { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; line-height: 1.5; }

  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .card { border: 3px solid var(--color-text); background: var(--color-surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-chunky); padding: var(--space-6); }
  .card.ways { background: var(--color-house-tint); }
  .card h2 { font-family: var(--font-family-read); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 0.95; margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; }
  .ticks, .waylist { list-style: none; margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .ticks li, .waylist li { font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 5px 0 5px 22px; position: relative; line-height: 1.4; }
  .ticks li::before { content: "✓"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-house-2); font-weight: 700; }
  .waylist li::before { content: "→"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-house-2); font-family: var(--font-family-mono); }
  .fine { font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-5); }

  .issues-cta { border: 3px dashed var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); padding: var(--space-6); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-6); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .issues-cta p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); max-width: 60ch; margin: 0; }

  .three { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .mini { border: 3px solid var(--color-border); background: var(--color-surface); padding: var(--space-5); }
  .mini p:last-child { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; line-height: 1.5; }
  .mini a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.15em; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) { .steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .two, .three { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
